    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors). The redesign is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and moved every value derived from it onto the new region-and-hash identity.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewritten. It now builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n- **REGION** derived from the owner's postcode (`NSW 2000-2099`, `VIC 3000-3099`, `QLD 4000-4099`, else `UNKNOWN`).\n- **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. The telephone is already E.164-normalized by `ValidateOwnerFields` before this step runs; last name is used as-is.\n- Sequence numbers dropped entirely, so the step no longer needs `OwnerRepository` or any cross-owner counting.\n\n**Values built from `customerCode` \u2014 automatically follow the new identity:**\n- **Membership number** (`OwnerMapper`, `<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and **check digit** (`CheckDigit` Luhn over the code's digits) already read `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so they now build on the region-and-hash code with no change.\n- **Create audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now emits the new code (verified in the run: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n**`Locality.java` + `OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the **locality derivation** moved onto the new identity. Instead of independently recomputing from postcode/city, `Locality.of` now returns the REGION component of the `customerCode` (the part before the first `-`), and `OwnerMapper` calls `Locality.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`.\n\n**Docs/cleanup:** updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples in `openapi.yml`, and corrected the `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` javadoc that referenced the removed per-city count.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` (asserting `customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) and the full suite pass.\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: REGION is derived **purely from the postcode** (per the spec's wording \"the region code derived from the postcode\"), with no city fallback. So an owner with a known city but no postcode now gets `UNKNOWN` rather than the city's region \u2014 a deliberate behaviour change from the old postcode-preferred-then-city logic. No test covers that case, but let me know if you'd prefer to keep the city fallback.",
